																		Abiogenesis SCP (Greenlight 2/2) 
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sputnik-one" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7005588&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607890625" alt="Sputnik One" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7005588)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sputnik-one" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;" >Sputnik One</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607546450 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Dec 2020 20:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840849">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Science-Fiction</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Classic SCP style, with addenda encompassing recovered mission logs.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP is an ancient spacecraft in a highly elliptical orbit around the Sun. Foundation exploration reveals that the spacecraft is in fact of human origin, but possesses technology that surpasses modern-day capabilities. A long deceased human crew are found within, and their mission logs shake the Foundation's view of what they think they know.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;details</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;details</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The spacecrafts mission logs detail the appearance of a spatial anomaly in the form of an Einstein–Rosen bridge (aka wormhole), that appeared in the outer reaches of the solar system in mid 21st century (the future from the perspective of the modern-day Foundation.) The Foundation in the future detected a planet on the other side, and emission spectroscopy implied that the planet may have been habitable. Foundation personnel were sent through after probes failed to return. The narrative follows the deceased crew through a series of mission logs. After entering the wormhole, they found themselves around a rocky planet, not dissimilar to our own.</p>
<p>One of the crew got in the lander to touch down on the planet and assess the habitability. Meanwhile, those that remained on the mothership performed scans of the solar system to check for other orbital bodies. The crew came to an astonishing revelation, the solar system wasn't dissimilar to our own. That's when they realised the wormhole didn't send them through space, it sent them through <em>time</em>. Approximately 4 billion years into the past. The ground crew landed on a primordial Earth, which they've unknowingly seeded with nucleotides, nucleases, bacteria etc. The wormhole then started to become unstable and so the crew in orbit made their way back. It was in vain, however, as the wormhole closed and they were left in a highly elliptical orbit around the sun, completely out of fuel. Modern day Foundation then find the ancient spacecraft in the present day, and the final log of the captain, detailing how he believed they kickstarted abiogenesis (life from non-life).</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Humanity inadvertently jump started life on Earth 4 billion years in the past. The unknowing astronauts mediated abiogenesis - life from non-life. All of Earth's life can be traced back to a single common ancestor, created through the highly unlikely and poorly understood event of abiogenesis. <em>This event</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The dead crew are alive in the present day, and so the Foundation trains them in preparation for the appearance of the wormhole.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<div style="background-color: #CBFAC1; margin: 1em 40px; padding: 0 1em; color: rgba(0,0,0,0.8); border: 1px solid #4FA23D;">
<p><span style="color: green"><strong>Edit:</strong> I've managed to secure 2 greenlights. Thank you to everyone who took the time to critique this and help me mould the concept into something that will (hopefully) be good!</span></p>
</div>

