<p>(Can’t give green lights)<br />
Firstly, I really like the idea. I’m a big of fan of sci-fi plots like this one and think this has a lot of potential.</p>
<p>Secondly, I think the plot of an article like this would really benefit from a personal perspective. Some logs detailing the captain’s and the foundation’s reaction to learning about the origin of life being from humans and how their ideas about the universe change. Perhaps you have the captain or researcher be a religious man, despite working with anomalies everyday. A realization such as this would force them to challenge their beliefs and would add to the intrigue of the story.</p>
<p>Being careful not to make the plot too convoluted or confusing in a story like this is also important. Keeping things simple yet intriguing will provide food for thought and cut down on questions that ruin this kind of plot.</p>

							</div>

								
