<p>I was going to leave up somewhat up to interpretation. One of the crew, for example, suggests it was God that created the wormhole. She cites the fact that the wormhole took 7 days to fully manifest, drawing parallels to Genesis in the Bible. Another member of the crew, however, states he thinks it was created by future humans (or perhaps even a future incarnation of the Foundation), who know about the event in the present, and therefore created the wormhole in the past to facilitate humanity creating themselves. The fact that the wormhole collapsed directly after they seeded the primordial Earth would support this, given the fact that interfering with the primordial Earth too much could lead to humanity never existing in the first place. Kind of like a paradox I guess?</p>
<p>Hahah, don't worry. There won't be any extra-galactic space cuttlefish that have come to purge the galaxy of sapient life.</p>
