<p>My, concern here is that it feels like this is kinda balancing on the knife edge between being really great and really boring with not a lot of margin for error if you don't nail the balance: like, to execute this well, you're really going to have to pull off an ambitious work blending characters and intrigue together in a way that'll be pretty challenging, and there's definitely the possibility that there's a huge section in the middle where not much happens; but I think as long as you manage to keep it tight and character focussed and really make it work, this could be good.</p>
